<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>04 · BENCHMARKS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Three benchmarks, each owning one hypothesis
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 1128, marginTop: 22 }}>
        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', background: '#16233A', padding: '12px 16px' }}>
            <Text style={{ width: 160, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Benchmark</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 470, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Tasks used here</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 350, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Protocol</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 148, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Owns</Text>
        </Box>
        {[
            ['PolyBench', '6 main-table tasks: Tg, Tm, modulus, permeability, dielectric loss, IWLT', 'Fixed 70/30 split × 3 seeds', 'H1'],
            ['PB26', '2 tasks (PolyMetriX Tg, homopolymer density) + official architecture transfer', 'Official 5-fold, seed 42', 'H2, H1-arch'],
            ['OpenPoly', '3 properties: Tg, Tm, dielectric constant', '5-fold × 3 seeds × 5 n-levels', 'H3, H4'],
        ].map(([name, tasks, protocol, owns]) => (
            <Box key={name} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', padding: '13px 16px', background: '#0E1728', borderBottom: '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Text style={{ width: 160, fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF' }}>{name}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 470, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>{tasks}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 350, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>{protocol}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 148, fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>{owns}</Text>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 44, marginTop: 8 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 470, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#93A8C2', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>POLYBENCH&apos;S OWN THREE TIERS</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 470, marginTop: 10 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', background: '#16233A', padding: '9px 14px' }}>
                    <Text style={{ width: 60, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>tier</Text>
                    <Text style={{ width: 210, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>tasks</Text>
                    <Text style={{ width: 172, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>labelled rows</Text>
                </Box>
                {[
                    ['1', 'Tg, Tm', '8,055 / 3,796'],
                    ['2', 'modulus, permeability', '1,034 / 711'],
                    ['3', 'dielectric loss, IWLT', '279 / 228'],
                ].map(([t, tasks, rows]) => (
                    <Box key={t} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', padding: '10px 14px', background: '#0E1728', borderBottom: '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                        <Text style={{ width: 60, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{t}</Text>
                        <Text style={{ width: 210, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{tasks}</Text>
                        <Text style={{ width: 172, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{rows}</Text>
                    </Box>
                ))}
            </Box>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', justifyContent: 'center', gap: 16 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 20, color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.5, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>
                Tier and sample size are nearly the same variable here: ρ = −0.956.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
                A tier label therefore carries two things at once — &quot;needs chain information&quot; and &quot;has 30× less data&quot;.
                We say so here, where the tiers appear, not in the discussion afterwards.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 980, gap: 2 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#8FA3BC', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                H1-arch, same row (RMSE, lower = easier). OOD: random 0.478 &lt; block 0.526 — block is the harder split, which is what we predicted.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#8FA3BC', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                ID: alternating 0.110 &lt; homopolymer 0.395 — homopolymer is harder, against it. Two domains; stated, not scored.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>5 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
